          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              monoidal
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            is the analogue of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mon%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} Mon(∞,1)Cat
          %p
            There are various ways to state the monoidal structure. One is in terms of fibrations over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em Noncommutative algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702299"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            Another is in terms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-operad
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Francis"} Francis
          %p
            Just as many ordinary
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
