            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#NikolausSagave15"} NikolausSagave15
          %h3#idea_of_the_simplicial_definition Idea of the simplicial definition
          %p
            As discussed at the end of the entry on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            may be thought of as a lax functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  * \to \mathbf{B} Cat
          %p
            from the terminal category to the one-object 3-category whose single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            of all categories and for which composition is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          %p
            More concretely, as also described there, such a lax functor is a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            object in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi lim
                      %mi Δ
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim^{\Delta} const_{\mathbf{B}Cat}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 4
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Cat
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mi Id
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 3
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi α
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Cat
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mi Id
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ⊗
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Cat
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mi Id
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Cat
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mi Id
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  F \Delta^4 &amp;\stackrel{=}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B} Cat
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow^{Id}
                  \\\
                  F \Delta^3 &amp;\stackrel{\alpha}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B} Cat
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow^{Id}
                  \\\
                  F \Delta^2 &amp;\stackrel{\otimes}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B} Cat
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow^{Id}
                  \\\
                  F \Delta^1 &amp;\stackrel{C}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}Cat
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow^{Id}
                  \\\
                  F\Delta^0 &amp;\stackrel{\bullet}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}Cat
                  }
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \Delta^n
            is the free 3-category of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            (an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriental"} oriental
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            and, in degree 4, the respect for the pentagon identity – and the condition is that this commutes for all vertical morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\Delta^n \to \Delta^m)
          %p So this is a 4-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F(\Delta^4) \to \mathbf{B}Cat
          %p subject to a certain constraint.
          %p
            Using the general mechanism of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo ⊗
                          %mo →
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mn 4
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C^\otimes \to F(\Delta^4)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            With a bit more time than I have on the train one can figure out that conversely suitable such fibrations are equivalent to monoidal categories. Alternatively, one can read pages 5 and 6 of
            %em LurieNonCom
            cited below.
          %p In any case, this motivates the following definition.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#plain_monoidal_category
            Plain monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                monoidal (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty,1
                )-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, \otimes)
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo ⊗
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\otimes
              %li
                %p
                  and a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+fibration"} coCartesian fibration
                  of simplicial sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo →
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_\otimes : C^\otimes \to N(\Delta)^{op}
              %li
                %p
                  such that for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  the induced
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} (infinity,1)-functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi i
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\otimes_{[n]} \to C^\otimes_{\{i,i+1\}}
                  determines an equivalence of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\otimes_{[n]}
                    \\to
                    C^\otimes_{\{0,1\}}
                    \\times
                    \\cdots
                    \\times
                    C^\otimes_{\{n-1,n\}}
                    \\simeq
                    (C^\otimes_{[1]})^n
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\Delta)
              its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
          %h3#monoidal_category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            \-monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The following defines
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-categories
            and their variants, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+operad"} commutative operad
            is replaced by any other
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-operad
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^\otimes
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-operad
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} coCartesian fibration of (∞,1)-operads
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+fibration"} coCartesian fibration
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : \mathcal{C}^\otimes \to \mathcal{O}^\otimes
                  of the underlying
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
              %li
                %p such that the composite
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi p
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Fin
                          %mo *
                        %mo =
                        %mi Comm
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{C}^\otimes \stackrel{p}{\to} \mathcal{O}^\otimes \to Fin_* = Comm
                %p
                  exhibits
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^\otimes
                  as an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operad"} (∞,1)-operad
            %p
              In this case we say that the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒪
                          %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}  = \mathcal{C}^\otimes \times_{\mathcal{O}^\otimes} \mathcal{O}
            %p
              is equipped by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              of an
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
                  \-monoidal
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 2.1.2.13
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              \=
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+operad"} Comm
              = succeed "-monoidal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
          %h2#higher_monoidal_structure Higher monoidal structure
          %p
            While for an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            there is just one notion of commutativity (either it is or it is not commutative), already a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            distinguishes between being just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided monoidal
            or fully
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
          %p
            This pattern continues, as expressed by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} periodic table of k-tuply monoidal categories
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category
            may be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-category
            or more generally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+%28n%2Cr%29-category"} k-tuply monoidal (n,r)-category
            for different values of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k= 1
            (since for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
            there is no monoidal structure at all) corresponds to monoidal product which is
            = succeed "-associative," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %em commutativity
          %p
            One says that an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em symmetric monoiodal
            if it is “as monoidal as possible”, i.e.
            = succeed "-tuply" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} Noncommutative algebra
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} Commutative algebra
            we have
          %ul
            %li
              %p the 1-fold monoidal (∞,1)-categories described here;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}> ∞-tuply monoidal (∞,1)-categories
                \.
          %h3#operadicalgebraic_definition_of_monoidal_structure Operadic/algebraic definition of monoidal structure
          %p
            For each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq n \leq \infty
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+n-disk+operad"} little n-disk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n^k
            of
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#Francis"} John Francis’ PhD thesis
            the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            equipped with an action of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            is established, so that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
